Installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.4.3) using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the children
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router integration

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):

1. **Framework Detection**: Identified this as a Next.js 16.2.12 project using the App Router pattern (has `src/app/layout.tsx`)
2. **Package Manager**: Confirmed npm is the package manager (presence of `package-lock.json`)
3. **Integration Pattern**: Used the Next.js App Router pattern by adding the Analytics component to the root layout file
4. **Placement**: Added `<Analytics />` at the end of the `<body>` tag to ensure proper tracking without interfering with page content

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No linting errors introduced in the modified file
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ All 23 routes generated without errors

## Next Steps (For Deployment)

To enable analytics data collection on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Select the project and click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. The tracking script will be available at `/_vercel/insights/*` routes after deployment
5. Verify by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` when visiting pages

## Notes

- The Analytics component is a wrapper around the tracking script that provides seamless Next.js integration
- It automatically supports Next.js routing and page tracking
- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking
- The component works in both development and production environments
